Local experimental checkpoint, 2026-10-01

Independent Luna production review at alloc.c ed19a77f73da71782717ab5b80748a513b985dbc4c3987ee8e8fb4dd893f91f7 found no remaining ownership/accounting blocker. It confirmed the unchanged ordinary highest-tail policy, shared tail/append implementation, highest fitting single-extent selection, before-start declines, and exact post-COW reserve/free/emergency/pending deltas. Production reviewer is not its author.

Availability limitation explicitly accepted for this bounded experiment by the primary agent: pre-start NOMEM from root validation, leaf scan or extra scratch storage is propagated rather than converted into ordinary retry. Extra scratch heap may fail where ordinary allocation could succeed. This is not a durability/accounting defect and is not a claim of unchanged low-memory availability. Corruption and physical IO must not be discarded, and post-start failures must never retry ordinary allocation.

Preserved V1 functional oracle compiled directly from its immutable evidence file against final V2 production: 16 pass, zero fail. Fresh V2 negative-control variants were derived from final ed19a77f source, not the earlier V1 mutants. Removing only the equal-live published-root guard fails exactly the corresponding preserved oracle; removing only optional pending-headroom guard fails exactly its corresponding oracle. Both runs report 15 pass and one expected failure. Variant source identities and exact patches are retained separately.

Existing focused regression gate: seven suites / 107 tests pass at final V2 production, including the original sealed-preflight oracles with their separately qualified actual-COW provenance helper. The initial wrong Make target invocation was retained and is not counted as a gate.

Two separate normal/probe m68k builds reproduce normal 2db1e1b7c0fae544d6eda24fa55342d528c6404e6b9aa6ddbf29283cf5ea5646 and probe eec8251eae5bcebfdb4cce2adceb9046123ea0b846c193f26bd44b50f53545b3. Local quality/static checks and Linux conformance plus actual FUSE pass. Fresh normal/probe emulator measurements started only after source review, preserved functional oracle, input identities and idle preflight; new V2-specific test authoring/full host qualification were still in progress. Measurements do not independently qualify safety or authorize retention.

No CI, push, PR, merge, release, real power-cut/controller-lie/hardware qualification or external publication was performed.

Main independent fault-test integration review at 242d97f8 identified that the artificial post-swap owner contradiction asserted the sticky field but did not yet exercise later rejection. The author added a subsequent NULL/AGAIN allocator call and AGAIN sync with unchanged write counts, after the published-root-byte witness. fs_sync checks recovery_error before entering commit, so this does not inspect or publish the deliberately contradicted pending queue. Final test source dd7103a5fcf30275f931197485a05eb6365753af9f532e951616c843a8519224 passes nine focused cases in a unique second build directory; its previous final logs were retained.

Historical fault-log limitation: the worker overwrote its immediately preceding failed run before reporting it; that log is unavailable. Its mistaken oracle expected iface->error() == OK after a successful retry, whereas the interface maps clear last_error to NOSPC. The correction requires the successful in-range returned block and last_error == OK. This unavailable historical attempt is disclosed and is neither reconstructed nor counted as qualification.

Main independently reviewed the expanded fault diff against the immutable V1 source: the new no-fit construction obtains every test-held/free block through actual allocator ownership, excludes historical emergency aliases, and proves all live extents are too short despite global reserve/headroom; its second-write failure is ordinary fallback, not a second batch COW. Those cuts retain exact first-progress root/free witnesses and the ordinary saved roving hint, pool distinctness, published bytes, successful retry and abandoned readonly committed graph/data checker. The new real mounted callback fault is explicitly artificial volatile-owner contradiction after successful physical scratch write/root swap. No valid-context reentry/power/controller claim is inferred. Passing fixture paths clean up; existing assertion-failure macros can bypass cleanup/unlock.

Independent Luna normal extraction agrees with all sixteen strict schema/data results and four-run means: create +40.899640%, write +29.948056%, delete +29.616174%, seventeen of twenty-four adverse matched BFS observations, twelve same-run candidate ratios over five. Its initially unlabeled raw-delta vectors put repeat BFS-first before repeat PFS3-first while ratio vectors used the opposite order; explicit named pairs clarified that ordering, not a calculation defect. All twenty-four labeled deltas and same-run ratios agree with the JSON and full measurement summary. Main decision: reject the V2 optional allocation policy, irrespective of reduced node counts.

Independent source mapping counts seven to eight root node_read invocations in a successful height-one batch. These are not physical reads or CRC computations: context-valid cache structure proof can return before CRC/structure validation. Preflight tag read precedes two full-scan root reads; selected update/delete reads again at mutation; postflight tag read precedes floor-search and overlap-scan reads. Existing API returns tags or transient key/value callbacks, not a retained validated root-leaf view. A within-call combined view would require explicit ordering/provenance semantics; no implementation or speedup is approved from static call counts alone.

