Final functional source 7fd2ecfb12b906488314475b115fa5b94668e42337b6bbcd32d8206b277f1088 passes eighteen focused tests. Initial pointer-type/diagnostic compile errors and false fresh-mount nonzero-stock/exact-leaf-capacity assumptions were corrected; their unique failed logs are retained and are not gates. The test obtains actual held blocks and queues them before sync, retains exact one-COW/delta assertions across seven block sizes, and supplements leaf capacity with actual caller-owned crumbs rather than weakening capacity checks. Final fault source dd7103a5 remains frozen.

Coverage limit: this functional file does not independently prove generic standalone eight-request warmup, empty mounted FreeTree or older root with nonzero initial reserve. The fault fixture only checks initial stock <=20 after its baseline commit, so its published-root retirement plus pending+1 witness does not establish a nonzero initial stock either. No exact older-root/nonzero-stock branch coverage is claimed. Existing generic allocator tests are included in the complete regression gate.

Complete final V2 normal and actual ASan/UBSan host suites both completed successfully. Source and test identities were frozen before compiling the two new files; the existing prebuild intentionally excluded moving tests. Explicit sanitizer flags are HOST_CFLAGS and leak detection is disabled. No production source changed during these builds.

Each complete run contains fifty suites and 487 cases, all passed. Independent final functional reviewer found no blocker; it noted that the no-fit call lacks an explicit pending-headroom assertion, although the default16384-slot cap and leaf-capacity-scale setup give a source-bound headroom argument. That is not presented as a direct callback witness.

